// The collaborative termination protocol on top of two_pc_timeout.ded (Bernstein, Hadzilacos and Goodman; LDFI §5.1:
// "CTP attempts to ameliorate the blocking problem by augmenting the 2PC protocol so as to allow agents who suspect
// that the coordinator has failed to exchange their knowledge about the outcome"). A participant that times out
// while prepared and undecided asks its peers. A peer that has decided answers with its decision; a peer that has not
// voted yet aborts unilaterally and answers abort; a peer that voted yes and is undecided is uncertain as well and
// cannot help, so CTP still has blocking executions. Used together with two_pc.ded, two_pc_timeout.ded and
// ../util/timer.ded. Blossom golden corpus, re-derived (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

arm_timer(A, "decision", X, 3) :- prepare(A, C, X), can(A, X);
knows(A, X) :- commit(A, X);
knows(A, X) :- abort(A, X);
decision_req(P, A, X)@async :- timeout(A, "decision", X), prepared(A, _, X), peer(A, P), notin knows(A, X);
commit(Q, X)@async :- decision_req(P, Q, X), commit(P, X);
abort(Q, X)@async :- decision_req(P, Q, X), abort(P, X);
abort(P, X) :- decision_req(P, Q, X), notin prepared(P, _, X);
